"preprint_date":"2020-11-14","author_count":3,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"16 pages, 3 figures, two-column revtex-4 format. Minor changes in the\n  abstract, introduction and discussion, appendix and references added, typos\n  corrected. Published in Physical Review D"}],"earliest_date":"2020-11-14","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"4212424"}],"facet_author_name":["1797180_Subhodeep Sarkar","1065349_Srijit Bhattacharjee","1261719_Arpan Bhattacharyya"],"core":true,"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1830603","updated":"2025-07-18T14:27:24.226612"},"journal_title_variants":["Phys. Rev. D","Phys.Rev.D"],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc","hep-th"],"value":"2011.08179"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["R.M.Wald.1","N.D.Birrell.1","Emanuele.Berti.1","E.Shaghoulian.1","A.Zhidenko.1","A.Achucarro.1","B.Bruegmann.1","R.B.Mann.1","Edward.Witten.1","Alex.Pandya.1","S.Sannan.1","Henry.W.Lin.1","C.Bunster.1","S.Hollands.1","Juan.M.Maldacena.1","P.Navarro.1","R.Petryk.1","P.Fiziev.1","Spenta.Rustom.Wadia.1","Da.Ping.Du.1","Maitraya.K.Bhattacharyya.1","M.G.Richarte.1","Ru.Keng.Su.1","H.R.Ruter.1","Thomas.E.Hartman.1","J.P.S.Lemos.1","A.R.Brown.1","K.D.Kokkotas.1","A.A.Costa.1","Cristian.Martinez.1","A.Tajdini.1","I.Sakalli.1","V.B.Bezerra.1","D.Birmingham.1","H.S.Vieira.1","Stephen.W.Hawking.1","F.Pretorius.1","Roman.A.Konoplya.1","S.Hod.1","M.V.Vishal.1","Vijay.Balasubramanian.1","H.Gharibyan.1","K.Rajesh.Nayak.1","Paul.C.W.Davies.1","S.B.Giddings.1","J.Zanelli.1","Sunil.Kumar.Sake.1","A.V.Saa.1","P.P.Fiziev.3","J.Polchinski.1","R.Ruffini.1","A.O.Starinets.1","S.P.Kumar.1","J.C.Fabris.1","A.Y.Shiekh.1","A.Strominger.1","T.J.Hollowood.1","V.E.Hubeny.1","D.V.Vassilevich.1","Pranjal.Nayak.1","A.Lopez.Ortega.1","B.G.Schmidt.1","J.Zahn.1","W.Kummer.1","R.Cordero.1","J.Navarro.Salas.1","H.S.Reall.1","Shailesh.Kumar.1","L.Tarasov.1","A.Ori.2","A.M.Sengupta.1","T.Damour.1","G.T.Horowitz.1","Bin.Wang.1","Upamanyu.Moitra.1","O.J.C.Dias.1","V.Cardoso.1","Subhodeep.Sarkar.1","D.Stanford.1","L.Thorlacius.1","S.Bhattacharjee.1","P.Breitenlohner.1","D.Grumiller.1","L.Susskind.1","D.Hilditch.1","A.Almheiri.1","C.G.Callan.1","S.Sachdev.1","D.Louis.Martinez.1","D.R.Staicova.1","G.Kunstatter.1","Ashish.Shukla.1","R.W.Jackiw.1","S.P.Trivedi.1","J.E.Santos.1","D.M.Marolf.1","M.Banados.1","I.Vega.Acevedo.1","D.Z.Freedman.1","Ronak.M.Soni.1","S.Shelemy.1","Jeffrey.A.Harvey.1","J.Kettner.1","G.Mandal.1","J.Ye.14","T.S.Levi.1","M.E.Ortiz.1","A.J.M.Medved.1","J.Gegenberg.1","Ying.Zhao.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"w0_btz1.png","caption":"Penrose diagram of a Ach\\'ucarro-Ortiz Black Hole: The blue region denotes the interoir of the black hole and the red region denotes the exterior. The future event horizon ($\\mathcal{H}^+_R$), the past event horizon ($\\mathcal{H}^-_R$) the right and left future Cauchy horizons ($\\mathcal{CH}^+_R$ and $\\mathcal{CH}^+_L$, respectively) have been indicated in the diagram. $\\mathcal{H}^+_L$ is the future even horizon of the other asymptotically $AdS$ region","source":"arxiv","key":"0adefd7a9a083c8bb7928134051608de","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/0adefd7a9a083c8bb7928134051608de"},{"filename":"pole.png","caption":"Schematic diagram of the contours of integration in the complex $\\w$ plane and the relevant poles. The pole marked in green is the slowest decaying right quasinormal mode. The remaining poles correspond to $\\w=-in\\k_-$, the ones marked in red contribute (smoothly) to the integral and the black ones do not.","source":"arxiv","key":"64e0aebfb8db92b7c91be5842f669990","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/64e0aebfb8db92b7c91be5842f669990"},{"filename":"w2_btz_quantum.png","caption":"The blue arrow denotes the integration path and the red arrows show the limit $v \\to \\infty$ as discussed while calculating the quantum stress energy tensor in two dimensions.","source":"arxiv","key":"a89f8b521dce662d2df1d686cff1b6f3","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a89f8b521dce662d2df1d686cff1b6f3"}],"legacy_version":"20210114073229.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Theory-HEP","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Theory-HEP"}],"first_author":{"emails":["srijuster@gmail.com"],"full_name":"Bhattacharjee, Srijit","last_name":"Bhattacharjee","first_name":"Srijit","recid":1065349},"control_number":1830603,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1103/PhysRevD.103.024008"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Bhattacharjee:2020nul"],"abstracts":[{"source":"APS","value":"We study linear scalar perturbations of black holes in two-dimensional (2D) gravity models with a particular emphasis on Jackiw-Teitelboim (JT) gravity. We obtain an exact expression of the quasinormal mode frequencies for single horizon black holes in JT gravity and then verify it numerically using the Horowitz-Hubeny method. For a 2D Reissner-Nordström like solution, we find that the massless scalar wave equation reduces to the confluent Heun equation using which we calculate the Hawking spectra. Finally, we consider the dimensionally reduced Bañados-Teitelboim-Zanelli (BTZ) black hole and obtain the exterior and interior quasinormal modes. The dynamics of a scalar field near the Cauchy horizon mimics the behavior of the same for the usual BTZ black hole, indicating a possible violation of the strong cosmic censorship conjecture in the near extreme limit. However, quantum effects seem to rescue strong cosmic censorship.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We study linear scalar perturbations of black holes in two-dimensional (2D) gravity models with a particular emphasis on Jackiw-Teitelboim (JT) gravity. We obtain an exact expression of the quasinormal mode frequencies for single horizon black holes in JT gravity and then verify it numerically using the Horowitz-Hubeny method. For a 2D Reissner-Nordstr\\\"om like solution, we find that the massless scalar wave equation reduces to the confluent Heun equation using which we calculate the Hawking spectra. Finally, we consider the dimensionally reduced Ba\\~nados-Teitelboim-Zanelli (BTZ) black hole and obtain the exterior and interior quasinormal modes. The dynamics of a scalar field near the Cauchy horizon mimics the behavior of the same for the usual BTZ black hole, indicating a possible violation of the strong cosmic censorship conjecture in the near extreme limit. However, quantum effects seem to rescue strong cosmic censorship.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Scalar perturbations of black holes in Jackiw-Teitelboim gravity"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2021-01-06"}],"curated":true},"id":"1830603","created":"2020-11-18T00:00:00+00:00"},{"updated":"2023-10-03T09:12:09.840655+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1837621?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1837621"},"metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"103","pubinfo_freetext":"Phys. Rev. D 103, 064077 (2021)","artid":"064077","material":"publication","year":2021,"journal_issue":"6","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.D"}],"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Applied Mathematics and Theoretical Physics, University of Cambridge , Wilberforce Road, Cambridge CB3 0WA, United Kingdom"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized